
@attribute [Route($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_DataTable}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Usage}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Basic_Usage}")]

<PageTitle>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Data_Table @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Usage_Basic</PageTitle>

<h1>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Data_Table @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Usage_Basic . . . In Progress . . .</h1>

<p>
    The following example is a basic setup, similar to the one I'd use with results retrieved from the server, however, I wouldn't be using 100K rows, 
    as in the example - quite the opposite. I'd retrieve as few rows as possible, so there's less for the user to have to go through.
</p>
<p>
    As this site is just hosted on GitHub Pages, I simply generated 100K rows rather than calling an API. As a side note, from years of experience, the maximum number of rows
    I'd ever want to retrieve from an API and pull down to a SPA is around 3K to 7K, depending on the number of columns - but generally those numbers are fast.
</p>
<p>
    For reasons beyond me, it seems to be in vogue to use 100K rows for demos, which, in my experience and opinion, is a little silly given that it's probably only around
    1% to 5% of applications that actually need 100K rows on screen for the user. But to keep you all happy ...
</p>


<div style="height:700px;">
    <DataTable TData="Contact" DataSource="@_dataSource" DefaultSortIndex="-1" Title="Contact Results" PagerBinding="@_pagerBinding" FilterRule="_filterRule">
        <Filter>
            <DebounceFilter HintText="Filters across first name, surname and country" RegexPattern="^[A-Za-z ]*$" OnDebounceFilterResult="HandleOnDebounce"
                            ValidationMessage="Invalid filter, filtering paused, letters and spaces only"  />
        </Filter>
        <TableColumns>
            <DataColumn DataProperty="c => c.ContactID"   DisplayName="Contact ID"    IsSortable="true" />
            <DataColumn DataProperty="c => c.GivenName"   DisplayName="First Name"    IsSortable="true" />
            <DataColumn DataProperty="c => c.FamilyName"  DisplayName="Surname"       IsSortable="true" />
            <DataColumn DataProperty="c => c.Country"     DisplayName="Country"       IsSortable="true" />
            <DataColumn DataProperty="c => c.DateOfBirth" DisplayName="Data of Birth" ColumnAlignment="ColumnAlignment.Centre" IsSortable="true" />
            <DataColumn DataProperty="c => c.Rate" DisplayName="Hourly Rate" IsSortable="true" CellFormat="C" ColumnAlignment="ColumnAlignment.End" />
        </TableColumns>
        <BottomPager>
         <Pager @bind-CurrentPage="@_pagerBinding.CurrentPage" AriaLabel="Two button pager" TotalItemCount="@_pagerBinding.TotalItemCount" CurrentItemCount="@_pagerBinding.CurrentItemCount" 
         ItemsPerPage="@_pagerBinding.ItemsPerPage" PagerSelectorType="PagerSelectorType.Button" ShowFirstLast="true" PageAlignment="PageAlignment.End" AddApplicationRole="true" />
        </BottomPager>
    </DataTable>
</div>

<p>
    The Data Table doesn't come with a pager or filtering mechanism — you simply add your own, or drop in the BlazorRamp Debounce Filter and Pager, as I've done here. 
    They all work together and make all the appropriate screen reader announcements for whatever's being used.
</p>
<p>
    I will at some stage be creating an advanced filter component that you will be able to drop into the data table filter slot, and/or for you to use your own adhoc tables.
</p>
<p>
    I haven't done any performance testing or tuning; the code just uses simple reflection without source generators, so I may revisit this. 
</p>



<div class="flex-content justify-content-between">
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Left_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_DataTable}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Usage}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_About}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Data_Table - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Usage_About</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
    <a class="@GlobalValues.Link_Button_Class @GlobalValues.Link_Button_Right_Arrow_Modifier" href="@($"{GlobalValues.Root_path_Components}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_DataTable}/{GlobalValues.Component_Path_Part_Usage}/{GlobalValues.Common_Page_Path_Virtualizing}")">
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
        <span>@GlobalValues.Component_Name_Data_Table - @GlobalValues.Common_Page_Title_Virtualizing</span>
        <span aria-hidden="true"></span>
    </a>
</div>




@code{

    private Func<Contact, bool>? _filterRule   = null;
    private PagerBinding         _pagerBinding = new(0, 0, 0, 10);
    private List<Contact>        _dataSource   = [];


    protected override async Task OnInitializedAsync()
    
        => _dataSource = await StaticData.GetContacts(100_000);
 
    private async Task HandleOnDebounce(DebouncedFilterResult debounceResult)
    {
        if (debounceResult.IsValid)
        {
            _filterRule = (data) => data.GivenName.Contains(debounceResult.FilterValue, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                                    || data.FamilyName.Contains(debounceResult.FilterValue, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase)
                                    || data.Country.ToString().Contains(debounceResult.FilterValue, StringComparison.OrdinalIgnoreCase);


            await InvokeAsync(StateHasChanged);
        }
    }
}
